vars {
  ~authBaseUrl=https://uat-mcdp-be.omfysgroup.com,
  ~baseUrl=https://uatmcdphcmplatform.omfysgroup.com,
  ~attendanceBaseUrl=https://uatmcdphcmplatform.omfysgroup.com,
  ~empCode=,
  ~authToken=
}

vars:secret [
  empPassword
]

docs {
  UAT environment.

  Two hosts, and only two. Verified by hand against the live services:

    authBaseUrl  uat-mcdp-be.omfysgroup.com          issues the token
                                                     POST /auth/token -> 200 + JWT
    baseUrl      uatmcdphcmplatform.omfysgroup.com   serves the attendance API
    attendanceBaseUrl  same host as baseUrl          kept because requests
                                                     reference both names

  Hosts that look plausible and are not:

    uat_mcdp_hcm.omfysgroup.com   accepts TCP, so it looks alive, but serves a
                                  front-end bundle and its certificate does not
                                  match the hostname. Underscores are not legal
                                  in a DNS hostname. Every request to it dies at
                                  CERTIFICATE_VERIFY_FAILED before any assertion
                                  can run.
    dev_mcdp_be.omfysgroup.com    same underscore problem, and it is DEV.

  Both were configured here previously and cost a full suite's worth of
  assertions, recorded as "untested" rather than failing loudly.

  empCode and empPassword are deliberately empty. empPassword is declared
  secret so Bruno keeps it out of the file entirely -- fill both in Bruno's own
  environment editor, never in this file. A working password has already been
  committed to this repository once; the point of leaving these blank is that
  it cannot happen by copying this file.

  authToken is written at run time by the auth request:
    bru.setEnvVar("authToken", res.body.token)
  Leave it empty. Every other request sends Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}.
}
